WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
Next we'll be covering seizures, but before we get into the specifics, I want to show you a short

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.400
video of what a seizure actually looks like in a real world setting. It can be a little unsettling

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:15.040
to watch someone lose control of their body, but seeing this now is one of the best ways to make

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:20.000
sure you don't freeze up if you ever witness it in person. While you watch, I want you to look

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.760
closely at the person's movements and their level of awareness. You might see the classic shaking

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.639
or jerky movements, but you might also notice moments where the person is just very still or

00:00:30.639 --> 00:00:36.000
has a glassy-eyed stare. Just take it in for a moment and then we will move to the next slide

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.799
to talk about exactly what is happening in the brain and how you can step in to help.

